{"diagnosis": "Loopback with divider 64 sent 0xa5 but recv_buf_data latched 0xe0, causing TRAP uart data mismatch got 0xe0 want 0xa5. Start-bit half-period check uses full cfg_divider at line 84, but data-bit and stop-bit waits at lines 90 and 97 use (cfg_divider >> 4), sampling ~16x too fast. This early sampling captures the start-bit as data and shifts recv_pattern, corrupting the byte to 0xe0.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,14 +89,14 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS (FAIL 0xdead cleared), loopback 0xa5 matches, no TRAP uart data mismatch"}

